{"name":"Emerald Rain","hex":"#80c872","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"emerald","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various green gemstones, especially a green transparent form of beryl, highly valued as a precious stone.","Emerald green, a colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a rich green colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/emerald"},{"term":"rain","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Condensed water falling from a cloud.","Any matter moving or falling, usually through air, and especially if liquid or otherwise figuratively identifiable with raindrops."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have rain fall from the sky.","To fall as or like rain."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rain"}],"entries":[{"title":"Emerald","blocks":[{"text":"Emerald is a gemstone and a variety of the mineral beryl (Be3Al2(SiO3)6) colored green by trace amounts of chromium or sometimes vanadium. Beryl has a hardness of 7.5–8 on the Mohs scale. Most emeralds have many inclusions, so their toughness is classified as poor. Emerald is a cyclosilicate. It occurs mainly in association with quartz, muscovite, albite, mica schist, Pyrite schorl, microcline, fluorite, smoky quartz and elbaite."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/B%C3%A9ryl_var._%C3%A9meraude_sur_gangue_%28Muzo_Mine_Boyaca_-_Colombie%29_2.jpg/330px-B%C3%A9ryl_var._%C3%A9meraude_sur_gangue_%28Muzo_Mine_Boyaca_-_Colombie%29_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emerald","wikidata":"Q43513"},{"title":"Rain","blocks":[{"text":"Rain or rainfall is a form of atmospheric precipitation composed of droplets of water aerosols that have condensed from atmospheric water vapor and fall by gravity. Depending on the intensity, rain can be described as a drizzle, a shower, a cloudburst or a downpour. It is also often accompanied by other weather phenomena such as strong wind (rainstorm) and lightning (thunderstorm), and may be mixed with hail/ice pellet, snow (sleet) and sandstorm. Rain is a major component of the water cycle and is responsible for depositing most of the fresh water on Earth. It provides water for hydroelectric power plants, crop irrigation, and suitable conditions for many types of ecosystems."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Hard_rain_on_a_roof.jpg/330px-Hard_rain_on_a_roof.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rain","wikidata":"Q7925"},{"title":"Shades of green","blocks":[{"text":"Varieties of the color green may differ in hue, chroma or lightness, or in two or three of these qualities. Variations in value are also called tints and shades, a tint being a green or other hue mixed with white, a shade being mixed with black. A large selection of these various colors is shown below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Shades_of_Green.svg/330px-Shades_of_Green.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_green","wikidata":"Q19847180"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Emeraude_gisements.jpg/500px-Emeraude_gisements.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Emeraude_gisements.jpg/1280px-Emeraude_gisements.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Emeraude_gisements.jpg/500px-Emeraude_gisements.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Main emerald producing countries","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEmeraude_gisements.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1